From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add the GalaxyCore GC4653 sensor driver

Add a mainline V4L2 subdev driver for the GC4653, a 2560x1440 10-bit
Bayer sensor used on several Ingenic T31 cameras. The mode register
sequence and the 26-step analogue gain table (seven registers per step)
come from the Ingenic vendor sensor driver.

The driver exposes a single 1440p30 mode with HBLANK/VBLANK, exposure,
analogue gain, and mirror/flip controls. The flip register sits behind
the 0x031d access latch, which the driver opens and closes around the
update.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc4653.c
@@ -0,0 +1,935 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * GalaxyCore GC4653 CMOS Image Sensor Driver
+ *
+ * The register sequences and gain table are adapted from the Ingenic
+ * vendor sensor driver (sensor_gc4653_t31).
+ */
+
+#include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
+#include <linux/i2c.h>
